/-!
# Supported Hom split injectivity for a complete flag bundle

Source: blueprint latest, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-an,
`thm-pur-localized-top-chern.proof.md`, Step 1
(blueprint: lem-pur-flag-pullback-injective).

The supported Hom groups are the canonical pro-etale `FunctorialCupH` groups from
`def-pur-supported-class-operations`.  The pullback is the normalized map induced
by the Cartesian closed-support square.  The theorem records its additive left
inverse for every closed support, twist, and cohomological degree.

-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry

namespace WeilConjectures.PurityFiniteSetting

/--
For every closed support, signed twist, and degree, pullback to the complete flag
bundle has an additive left inverse on the canonical supported Hom groups.

Source: blueprint latest, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-an,
`thm-pur-localized-top-chern.proof.md`, Step 1
(blueprint: lem-pur-flag-pullback-injective).

Proof (source step by step):
1. For ranks zero and one, the complete flag bundle is the identity by
   `def-pur-complete-flag-bundle`, so the pullback and its retraction are identities.
   For higher rank, recurse through the projective bundle of the tautological
   kernel; `lem-pur-projective-bundle-tautological-geometry` supplies the
   geometric hypotheses and base-change identifications at each stage.
2. `lem-asd-etale-finite-twist-pullback`, `lem-pur-kummer-additivity`, and the
   derived tensor-pullback comparison transport every signed finite twist through
   the tower, including negative powers.  The ordinary/pro-etale comparison gives
   the same coefficient identifications on the pro-etale site.
3. Apply the projective-bundle formula successively.  Projection to the all-zero
   summand gives a retraction of the adjunction unit.
4. The finite-coefficient compact-support projection formula makes this retraction
   additive and natural after tensoring with an arbitrary target complex; the
   adjunction triangle identity gives retraction composed with the unit equal to
   the identity.
5. The normalized supported-Hom identification and its pullback compatibility
   identify this unit map with `functorialCupPullback`, so the induced additive map
   is a left inverse on every supported Hom group.  No regularity of the support
   is used.
6. Pullback and direct-image composition comparisons identify the recursive tower
   with the complete flag bundle and its all-zero projection.
-/
theorem flag_pullback_split_injective_statement (P : PurityFiniteSetting.{u})
    (r : ℕ) (T : Scheme.{u}) (F : T.Modules)
    [F.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank r] (bT : T ⟶ Spec (.of P.field.k))
    [IsSeparated bT] [LocallyOfFiniteType bT] [QuasiCompact bT]
    {Z Z' : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ T) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (i' : Z' ⟶ (completeFlagBundle r T F).scheme) [IsClosedImmersion i']
    (g : Z' ⟶ Z)
    (_sq : ChosenCartesianSquare g i' i (completeFlagBundle r T F).projection)
    (a b : ℤ) :
    ∃ s : P.FunctorialCupH true i' b a →+ P.FunctorialCupH true i b a,
      ∀ x : P.FunctorialCupH true i b a,
        s (P.functorialCupPullback true i i'
          (completeFlagBundle r T F).projection g _sq bT b a x) = x := by
  sorry

end WeilConjectures.PurityFiniteSetting
